# What the Vercel CLI must NOT upload.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `vc deploy --prebuilt` walks the project and decides for itself what to send. A local
# `rust/target` is gigabytes of build output that nothing in the deployed artifact needs — the wasm the browser
# fetches is the committed `public/rust-ui/ui_bg.wasm`, and the server is built inside its own Linux container from
# `rust/Dockerfile.vercel`. Letting the CLI consider 20 GB it does not need is how a deploy turns into
# "Upload aborted / fetch failed" with a retry storm, which is exactly what happened.
#
# These are all local-only trees: build output and personal data exports. None of them is referenced by the app at
# runtime, and none is in Git.

# Rust build output. The deploy ships the COMMITTED wasm, never anything from here.
rust/target

# Local data exports / working trees that live outside Git.
contact-export
apple-messages-export
gsd-core
praxis
.venv
data

# Build/type-check caches that are regenerated locally.
.next/cache
.turbo
coverage
